## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of CORS risks and practical mitigations in a fintech SPA context, focusing on per-origin controls, token usage, and incident response.

## Key Concepts
- CORS headers and policies
- Token-based auth and JWTs
- CI/CD security checks for config
- Incident response for cross-origin abuse

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example snippet for server CORS config (pseudo)
const allowedOrigins = ['https://app.example.com','https://admin.app.example.com'];
app.use((req,res,next)=>{ 
  const origin = req.headers.origin;
  if (allowedOrigins.includes(origin)) { res.setHeader('Access-Control-Allow-Origin', origin);
     res.setHeader('Access-Control-Allow-Credentials','true');
     res.setHeader('Access-Control-Allow-Methods','GET,POST,OPTIONS');
  } else { res.status(403).send('origin not allowed'); }
  next();
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you automate detection of misconfig in CI?
- How would you validate that CORS policies don’t block legitimate cross-origin traffic?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical supply‑chain security in a multi‑cloud setup, emphasizing tools, policy gates, and a ready IR workflow.

## Key Concepts

- Software supply chain integrity: SBOMs, attestation, and signed artifacts
- CI/CD gates: pre-deploy checks and fail-fast defaults
- Runtime controls: policy-driven attestation and anomaly detection
- IR readiness: rapid containment, evidence collection, and rollback

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo CI gate: verify SBOM presence and image signature
const bomExists = fs.existsSync('bom.json');
const sigVerified = verifyCosignSignature('image@sha256:…');
if (!bomExists || !sigVerified) {
  throw new Error('Unverified image: SBOM or signature missing');
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure success and ensure ongoing compliance as dependencies evolve?
- Which telemetry and dashboards would you implement to detect anomalies in supply chain events?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical, production-ready supply chain security controls across multi-cloud Kubernetes, focusing on SBOMs, artifact signing, and rapid IR.

## Key Concepts

- SBOMs and risk scoring
- Code signing with Cosign and KMS-backed keys
- CI secrets scanning
- Image-signature enforcement at admission
- 24h IR playbook and rollback

## Code Example

```javascript
// verify artifact signature (pseudo)
const crypto = require('crypto');
function verifySignature(blob, signature, publicKeyPem) {
  const verify = crypto.createVerify('SHA256');
  verify.update(blob);
  verify.end();
  return verify.verify(publicKeyPem, signature);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you rotate and revoke keys in flight without downtime?
- How would you integrate Sigstore or a private CA with this workflow?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates a candidate's ability to design concrete, layered security controls for a common integration risk in SaaS platforms. It tests understanding of both transport-layer and application-layer protections.

## Key Concepts
- Webhook signature verification using HMAC
- Replay protection via timestamps and narrow validation windows
- Secret management and rotation policies
- Transport security with mutual TLS (mTLS)

## Code Example
```javascript
const crypto = require('crypto');

function verifyWebhookSignature(payload, secret, signature, timestamp, windowMs = 300000) {
  const now = Date.now();
  if (now - timestamp > windowMs) return false;
  const data = \`${timestamp}.${payload}\`;
  const expected = crypto.createHmac('sha256', secret).update(data).digest('hex');
  return crypto.timingSafeEqual(Buffer.from(signature), Buffer.from(expected));
}
```
